{"title": "Australian energy giant signs up car subscription platform to manage EV fleet and V2G", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/06/01/australian-energy-giant-signs-up-car-subscription-platform-to-manage-ev-fleet-and-v2g/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/06/01/australian-energy-giant-signs-up-car-subscription-platform-to-manage-ev-fleet-and-v2g/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Australian energy giant signs up car subscription platform to manage EV fleet and V2G\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/KarmoCar-3-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Australia’s largest car subscription platform signs deal with energy giant to manage its electric vehicle subscription fleet and platform operations, and also to explore rollout of V2G.</p>\n<p>The agreement could also result in Karmo managing AGL's participation in vehicle-to-grid (V2G) technology, which allows EVs to contribute power back to the energy system and deliver additional value to customers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/06/01/australian-energy-giant-signs-up-car-subscription-platform-to-manage-ev-fleet-and-v2g/\">Australian energy giant signs up car subscription platform to manage EV fleet and V2G</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-31T22:21:42+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-06-01T10:11:26.772675+00:00"}
{"title": "Australian firm debuts vehicle-to-vehicle fast charging platform for stranded and remote EV drivers", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/06/01/australian-firm-debuts-vehicle-to-vehicle-fast-charging-platform-for-stranded-and-remote-ev-drivers/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/06/01/australian-firm-debuts-vehicle-to-vehicle-fast-charging-platform-for-stranded-and-remote-ev-drivers/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Australian firm debuts vehicle-to-vehicle fast charging platform for stranded and remote EV drivers\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Alpine-Energy-MGEN-M40-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Australian energy and technology company has debuted a potentially first-of-its-kind vehicle-to-vehicle DC fast charging platform, for stranded drivers or for remote mining operations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/06/01/australian-firm-debuts-vehicle-to-vehicle-fast-charging-platform-for-stranded-and-remote-ev-drivers/\">Australian firm debuts vehicle-to-vehicle fast charging platform for stranded and remote EV drivers</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-31T21:26:43+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-06-01T10:11:26.772675+00:00"}
